00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.511
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:00.570
Visal, who is a leader you admire?

68
00:04:01.683 --> 00:04:06.704
Our team captain. Leading by example, she inspired the whole team.

69
00:04:07.817 --> 00:04:09.050
What did she do?

70
00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:14.657
Listening carefully to everyone, she delegated tasks fairly.

71
00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.227
And when things went wrong?

72
00:04:18.317 --> 00:04:22.966
Staying calm, she changed the plan. She showed real adaptability.

73
00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.786
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:29.915
Grammar focus: Non-finite clauses.

75
00:04:30.215 --> 00:04:31.495
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:32.183 --> 00:04:35.309
Leading by example, she inspired the whole team.

77
00:04:36.217 --> 00:04:39.168
Listening carefully, he delegated tasks fairly.

78
00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:43.023
Inspired by her coach, she became a leader.

79
00:04:43.967 --> 00:04:49.231
The non-finite clause has no subject of its own. It shares the subject of the main clause.

80
00:04:49.983 --> 00:04:54.725
Be careful! Don't say: Lead by example, she inspired the team.

81
00:04:56.667 --> 00:05:00.048
Say: Leading by example, she inspired the team.

82
00:05:00.348 --> 00:05:02.939
A non-finite clause starts with the -ing form.

83
00:05:03.733 --> 00:05:06.177
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

